Coinbase announced strong Q3 2025 earnings, reporting $1.44 EPS and $1.86 billion in revenue—beating estimates by over 29%. The “x402” reference likely points to analyst price targets, with one projecting $404 and another $425.
Here’s a breakdown of Coinbase’s Q3 2025 performance and the context around “x402”:
📊 Financial Highlights
Earnings per Share (EPS): $1.44, beating the $1.11 estimate by 29.38%.
Revenue: $1.86 billion, up from $1.2 billion last year and above the $1.79 billion consensus.
Net Income: $433 million; Adjusted Net Income was $421 million.
Adjusted EBITDA: $801 million, signaling strong operational efficiency.
Trading Volume: $295 billion, up from $185 billion in Q3 2024.
🧠 Strategic and Operational Notes
Coinbase emphasized its progress toward building the “Everything Exchange,” a unified platform for all asset types.
Operating expenses dropped 9% quarter-over-quarter, while full-time employees increased 12% to 4,795.
📈 Analyst Price Targets & “x402”
JP Morgan’s Kenneth Worthington upgraded Coinbase to “Overweight” with a price target of $404 by December 2026.
HC Wainwright raised its target to $425, citing bullish crypto trends and regulatory tailwinds.
Barclays maintained “Equal Weight” but slightly lowered its target from $365 to $361.
So “x402” likely refers to the cluster of price targets around the $400 mark, signaling strong institutional confidence in Coinbase’s trajectory.
